{"Zoom adapter switched from zoomRefreshedTokenSchema.safeParse(responseBody) to parseRefreshTokenResponse(responseBody, zoomRefreshedTokenSchema), but the helper returns the parse wrapper rather than the token object that downstream code expects": 0.6458045244216919, "Google refresh path routes through the new helper but then parses the stale credential object or assumes the wrong response shape, so synced refresh responses can be ignored and stale tokens persisted": 0.7990442514419556, "Office365 refresh path mixes the new sync helper with the old parse-result contract, so it can parse the wrong response shape or mishandle token updates when sync mode returns only minimal token data": 0.7917938232421875, "Credential-sync webhook/auth constants do not match the documented .env.example names, so deployments using the advertised CALCOM_WEBHOOK_* settings can leave the feature disabled or cause every webhook request to be rejected": 0.12852743268013, "The app-credential webhook directly calls appCredentialWebhookRequestBodySchema.parse(req.body) without guarding for malformed payloads - req.body can be a string or undefined depending on content-type/body parsing, causing 500 zod errors instead of controlled 400/403 responses": 0.8795323371887207, "Webhook handler writes appId: appMetadata.slug instead of the app record's database id when persisting credentials, causing synced credentials to not match existing credential queries/relations": 0.40736424922943115, "Example credential-sync client posts { appSlug, encryptedKey } but the webhook route expects { userId, appSlug, keys } and sends userId as a query parameter to a different endpoint, causing schema validation errors or 404/400 responses": 0.4562292695045471, "parseRefreshTokenResponse switches to a minimum schema in sync mode, so provider-specific refresh fields can be omitted or no longer validated even though downstream code still depends on the full token payload": 0.8448591232299805, "Credential-sync refresh helper posts application/x-www-form-urlencoded data with calcomUserId and appSlug, but the webhook expects JSON body with userId, appSlug, and encrypted keys - the helper never sends the encrypted payload and uses different request-field names": 0.6532289981842041, "Webhook secret comparison compares req.headers[...] directly without handling that header values can be string | string[] | undefined, so a duplicated header arriving as an array can bypass intended error handling": 0.5596557855606079, "refreshOAuthTokens wrapper returns a raw Response when syncing is enabled, but if the sync endpoint returns a body that does not match the original provider schema exactly, later parsing and token updates can fail or overwrite the credential with incomplete data": 0.7650156617164612, "Salesforce calendar refresh path now uses inconsistent direct refresh/error handling and treats parseRefreshTokenResponse as a Zod result, so legitimate refreshes or sync-mode responses can be mishandled": 0.8095091581344604, "Salesforce CRM refresh path parses response with parseRefreshTokenResponse but still assumes normal OAuth JSON body - in sync mode the helper only enforces access_token plus some number field, so malformed provider error bodies can slip into different exception paths": 0.5887277126312256}